+# KithMoot node host integration candidate
+
+This host profile is a private engineering candidate. It does not publish
+Shelter, add a public catalogue entry or qualify an installed Archy node.
+
+The node requires Linux Archy on a rented server or remote host, an assigned
+public IPv4 address, a public DNS hostname and a current matching certificate
+covering both that name and `turn.<name>`. Obvious private and carrier-grade
+addresses are refused. This is not an ISP or home-connection detector.
+The host nginx stream module must already be installed.
+
+## Boundaries
+
+The app runs as container UID1000 with manifest-owned persistent data and three
+generated secrets. It receives no host certificate key. The host owns TLS,
+nginx routing and its private recovery journal.
+
+| Surface | Port or path |
+| --- | --- |
+| Node supervisor HTTP, loopback | 3750 |
+| Node Spry control HTTP, loopback | 3751 |
+| Node Shelter WebSocket, loopback | 3752 |
+| Node companion UI, loopback app gate | 3753 |
+| Node native TURN UDP/TCP | 34790 |
+| Host native TLS gate to node TURN | 53499 to34790 |
+| Node allocation range | UDP49192:49223 |
+| Node HTTPS/WSS and TURN TLS | 443 |
+
+The existing private Spry3744/3745,3478/5349 and49160:49191 are retained.
+The native gate recognises only the exact declared Spry and node mappings.
+
+Nginx uses SNI to send only `turn.<name>` to the fixed node TLS gate. Other TLS
+connections reach its existing dashboard or exact node HTTPS vhost over a
+private Unix socket. Trusted PROXY metadata preserves the original client
+address for the dashboard's source checks. Public callers and other app gates
+cannot supply that metadata. The native header parser is bounded and discards
+addresses after validation. TURN still authenticates each admitted device.
+
+Only the node's declared HTTPS API and `/events` are forwarded. Cookies,
+dashboard bearer credentials, CSRF headers and unrelated headers are withheld;
+only a syntactically scoped Nostr authorization header passes. Set-Cookie is
+removed from responses. Unknown paths and query strings are refused. Node HTTP,
+WebSocket and stream access logs are off; native TLS errors omit participant
+addresses. This does not change normal dashboard logging.
+
+## Lifecycle
+
+Preflight checks the existing private dashboard, public certificate and
+recognised nginx layout before app setup. Successful start activates host
+routing. A root-only journal records original and expected configuration
+hashes before any switch. Failed or killed applies restore the old configuration
+before retrying. A successful reload requires a new nginx worker generation
+and a real private HTTPS dashboard response with normal certificate and
+hostname verification. Operator-modified files are preserved and require review.
+
+A managed tmpfiles rule recreates nginx's private socket directory on boot.
+The daemon checks an installed profile's public certificate every30seconds.
+A complete valid renewal reloads nginx; the app gate reloads the same host
+certificate source. Incomplete renewal retains the last working pair and
+records a fixed host diagnostic without room or participant information.
+An absent node profile performs no privileged refresh.
+
+Destructive uninstall first requests the private local node's durable deletion
+intent. Existing rooms or pending closure prevent it. New enrolment stays frozen
+after a positive acknowledgement, including after restart. Host routing is
+restored before declarative container teardown. Retaining app data still removes
+the host route, without forging a keeper closure or erasing retained rooms.
+An operator can explicitly cancel deletion using the node's local control CLI.
+
+## Evidence gates
+
+The focused `archipelago-node-ingress-tests` harness imports the production
+TLS source. Its adapter supplies only the certificate fields consumed by that
+source; it does not replace production Config validation. Run through
+`scripts/test-backend-isolated.sh` with the corresponding
+`ARCHY_TEST_PACKAGE`. Shared native transport guards are tested through the
+`archipelago-container` package. Python renderer tests use the actual shipped
+dashboard configuration.
+
+`scripts/qualification/kithmoot-node-nginx.py` is destructive and explicitly
+restricted to its disposable offline Linux fixture. It exercises real nginx,
+production Rust TLS/native relay code and the production node/backends/SDK.
+Its generated CA is a fixture trust root. It does not qualify public CA issuance,
+external reachability, the full daemon, FIPS, system reboot or a physical phone.
+
+The private app package, full Archy install/start/stop/update/delete/reboot
+acceptance, independent NATs, forced TLS443 media and capacity remain separate
+gates. Published signed distribution and complete native licence notices are
+also required before a public install is offered.
+
+Maintainer must review and approve UI work on the Archy install, launch,
+pairing hand-off, delete-everything and status screens, and dashboard access
+alongside the node, before merging or approval. ZAT pending.
